    "done_when": "Read §7's psi-store paragraph and docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-reference-scope.html first. A converter module, imas_ambix/data/geqdsk_store.py, reads a shot's G-EQDSK through imas_ambix/challenge/loader.py load_geqdsk. It writes the psi grid as stored (COCOS 1, Wb/rad), its R and Z coordinate arrays and its time into a per-shot store group the transform engine reads. The group is zarr, sits under a cache root it is given, outside any fetched EDDB category, and uses the layout imas_alambic.eddb's cache writer uses, so the engine reads it like any channel. One rule in /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/maps/jt-60sa/maps/equilibrium.json binds that array to equilibrium/time_slice/profiles_2d/psi with transformation psi_like and source_cocos 1, and binds the grid coordinates where the rule system requires them, with an evidence string citing the G-EQDSK. packages/imas-alambic/src/imas_alambic/pulse_writer.py IDS_NAMES gains equilibrium, and tests/data/test_pulse_writer.py follows. Tests in tests/data/test_geqdsk_store.py build the store in tmp_path from the real /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/101011.geqdsk, which is read-only, and make §7's psi check. E101011's psi, minted through the engine at the G-EQDSK's time, agrees on the G-EQDSK grid with the G-EQDSK psi multiplied by -2 pi, to a normalised RMS difference under 1% of that psi's range. The same comparison with the rule's sign flipped exceeds it. Nothing under /work is written. Write the landing fragment docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-geqdsk-psi-store.html, quoting the rule and the measured difference. On the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set), with the worktree's maps a symlink to the main checkout's maps/, run in the foreground and capture once, to a log in the run directory whose first lines give the committed revision the tests ran at and the command, and whose last line is EXIT=: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/data/test_geqdsk_store.py tests/data/test_pulse_writer.py tests/data/test_jt60sa_signal_maps.py; it exits 0, and uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
